Spec: MitM Data Aggregator

Purpose:
  Provision of a reliable, secure, and decoupled system that collects data from various source systems, buffers it, aggregates it daily into JSON packages, and transmits it via a REST interface to a target SaaS solution.

Platform: Go,Rust/Linux

Owns:
  ./**

Must:
  All PII (Personally Identifiable Information) data is encrypted at-rest using Envelope Encryption (AES-GCM).
  The Master Key (KEK) is never persisted to disk.
  Child processes (collectors, deliverers, etc.) dynamically fetch the KEK and DB credentials via the IPC Unix Socket from the Scheduler.
  Each layer component is compiled as an independent Go binary with its own go.mod.
  Progress and cursors are tracked strictly in PostgreSQL.
  Child processes communicate status and audit events back to the scheduler via a nil-safe IPC socket.
  All code documentation and comments are in English.
  Every source file includes a standardized SPDX header (C++ style block comment) with Apache-2.0 license.
  The system is deployed as immutable Docker containers running in AWS ECS.
  Updates to executables or core configurations require a complete CI/CD deployment of a new container image.

Must not:
  Implement mechanisms for hot-swapping, uploading, or dynamically modifying executables at runtime.

References:
  ./docs/SpecDD_SpecKit_Integration_EN.md
